  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The major components of photochemical smog are nitrogen oxides, ozone <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PAN</mi></math> (peroxyacetylnitrate), and chemical compounds that contain the-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CHO</mi></math>&nbsp;group (aldehydes). <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PAN</mi></math> and aldehydes can cause eye irritation and plant damage if their concentrations are sufficiently high.</p><p>Classical smog occurs in a cool, humid climate. Its components include smoke, fog and sulphur dioxide. It is reducing in nature.</p></blockquote>"
